From: Daniel Mentz <danielmentz@google.com>
Date: Fri Sep 11 19:39:48 2026 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: KVM: arm64: iommu: Reject identity domain in kvm_iommu_free_domain

The identity mapping domain is a special hypervisor-internal domain that
mirrors the host stage-2 page tables and is intended to live for the
lifetime of the hypervisor.

Reject any attempt to free KVM_IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDMAP_ID in
kvm_iommu_free_domain().

Fixes: 1a45ce72b0cf ("ANDROID: KVM: iommu: Restrict access KVM_IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDMAP_ID")
Bug: 527169856
Assisted-by: Antigravity:gemini
Change-Id: I890141c746b7d0711eafda772d91f8576bf75c79
Signed-off-by: Daniel Mentz <danielmentz@google.com>

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common d4e462b6d55717be29fb2fadb2c40eefd18f3d5a
Batch: B-2 (P4 kvm/pKVM cluster) - Class A, apply as-is; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
index 1372848..84d4123 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/iommu/iommu.c
@@ -411,6 +411,9 @@ int kvm_iommu_free_domain(pkvm_handle_t domain_id)
 	int ret = 0;
 	struct kvm_hyp_iommu_domain *domain;
 
+	if (domain_id == KVM_IOMMU_DOMAIN_IDMAP_ID)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	domain = handle_to_domain(domain_id);
 	if (!domain)
 		return -EINVAL;
